# Karlov Watchdog: "Permanents your opponents control can't be turned face up during your turn." (CR 101.2, 708.7). Bot1 casts the Watchdog on turn 1. Bot2 casts
# Bolrac-Clan Basher face down on turn 2 (a Black Lotus pays the {3}) and keeps five Moxen untapped for its disguise cost {3}{R}{R}. On Bot1's turn 3 the cost is paid in
# full (the pool shows it) and Bot2 is still refused the special action, so the creature stays a face-down 2/2. On Bot2's own turn 4 the same cost turns it up: a 3/2
# Bolrac-Clan Basher with double strike and trample.

